from central banks it was a relatively  small amount  but for those from whom it was taken it  was obviously their life's uh savings  and and work  and valuables  and we have determined absolutely  specifically  uh that not only based on the pattern  and practice  of reich bank uh transactions and this  intermingling of monetary and  non-monetary gold  but from an analysis of prussian mint  smelting of looted dutch gilders from ss  victims  we know that some of that went abroad to  switzerland italy  we also know  from  other reports  and from the fact that some ss loot from  victims including gold coins  and bars were transferred by the allies  into the gold pool  there's also a question although we need  more information on this  about gold from  the nazi concentration camp of teresa  all of these uh  indicate  that victim gold was included and  therefore was redistributed but we do  not know the amounts  now in terms of the reich bank records  it's only within the last few weeks that  we really began to examine those the  reason being  that we had some 15 million pages of our  own documents  this is one of the reasons why we're  suggesting the possibility of an  international conference  we did find  after a great deal of examination that  we had  partial records  on microfilm  in the treasury department of reif bank  records and we discovered that only a  few weeks ago  those will be uh very important these  are part of the analysis this blow up  what seems to be missing  uh is that portion of the records  representing the full accounting of the  melmer ss  account  we have uh  very very clear indications  uh and bill correct me if i'm incorrect  here but we have very clear indications  from even the army  person who transferred  these uh records after they were given  to the united states for copying  and then transferred them back  uh that he that that this person did  deliver these particular records  uh  initially the rife bank said it's not  been able to identify those but they  certainly have not  uh at this point made a a full uh  examination and it will be very  important to get those  ss  account records from the reif bank and  i'm sure that they'll be cooperative try  to uh or did you did you look through  the files to see if reichsbank officials  who not only survived the war some of  them went to switzerland some of them  may have even stayed in germany  were ever uh deposed and and questioned  about this particular thing  they were deposed um i believe bill it  was mr poole  the vice  the vice chair  of the reich bank who provided very  crucial information to the army  uh after the uh after the war  it's also important in terms of getting  a sense of the that these are not dry  figures to just understand  the army almost uh inadvertently landed  on  this because the reich bank and the  closing weeks of the war transferred  almost all of their reserves into a salt  mine called the merker's mine  and as the allies swept through  germany  and the closing days of the war they  discovered in this salt mine  the this enormous uh gold pool  from reich bank records  and it's there that they found  the melmer account  it's there that they found  sacks  and box loads  of  victim gold identified by particular  concentration camps  and then in interviewing bill mr poole i  think it was  and others about the practice that they  had it was determined that this  re-smelting  operation was occurring both with  respect to central bank gold from the  other countries to disguise its origin  and to convert into usable tradable form  the victim's goal that uh this was  discovered bill do you want to add  anything on that  what were the four countries that you  say have claims on the uh uh tripartite  gold well there are 10 countries that  have claims  but uh the the countries that have i  think the the biggest claims are france  um  austria  the netherlands  and italy and how much of the 70 million  uh you said this twice that a  substantial portion of that 70 million  should be put in a account for survivors  or victims  can you be a little bit more specific  now we use that term because we want to  be able to uh discuss with our  allies  and the claimant countries the amounts  that ought to be done this has to be  done voluntarily  if we're going to do it in any  reasonable period of time to help the  survivors  we have stated our view we're not trying  to  pin other countries at this point to  to our negotiating position but that  that is our view  and we hope substantial means genuinely  a substantial amount of that and again i  think there's both a legal and a moral  basis and that this report helps  establish the legal basis for that  in examining  how much of this victim's gold may have  gone uh to switzerland either through  some kind of official way or even fenced  again because we can't quantify the  amount of victim gold we can't determine  what we do know is that some amount went  yes i think switzerland neutrality  during the war did you i mean is it  was there any comparison between the  amount of  money um and transactions switzerland  was handling for nazi germany  and the transactions it was handling for  for the allies  uh the swiss uh in fact uh bought very  substantial amounts by one uh  indication of the swiss national bank  they actually may have purchased more  gold from the allies than they did from  germany  uh and there was also some limited trade  although most of the trade was with uh  with germany okay one last question here  thank you  to follow on the non-military gold used  in the reports that states that there's  no evidence that switzerland italy knew  about the fact that there was  non-military gold but what is your  impression as an historian and yourself  mr eisenstein do you think that it's  possible that switzerland knew about it  i mean what  well again there is no question that  switzerland knew despite their initial  protestations of the country after the  war  uh there's no question that they knew  that there was looted gold we have  certainly uncovered no evidence that  they knew that it was victim's goal we  have no way of of making any judgment  beyond the fact that we have no evidence  in that respect and that the gold was  basically by  uh  by its appearance indistinguishable and  in again unfortunately the us definition  of non-monetary versus monetary goals  for tgc purposes was based on appearance  and not origin so all we can say is we  have no evidence  that would indicate that they knew it  was victims gold but there is clear  evidence they knew  that it was looted gold thank you very  much  you
 

